recipe audio: a PCM output stream: a sine tone queued per frame, playhead from queued()

A 440 Hz sine at 48 kHz stereo through `game.openAudioStream`: each frame tops the queue up to
N ms ahead and prints the playhead. Headless (no window); in a game put the top-up in the
frame callback.

The pieces:
- `game.openAudioStream(rate, channels)` opens its own SDL device for f32 interleaved samples
  (512-frame device buffer). `raw == 0` means no device: every call on it is then a no-op.
- `s.queue(samples)` appends `frames * channels` floats and never blocks. Queue ~30-N ms ahead
  each frame; more is latency, less risks gaps on a slow frame.
- Playhead in frames = frames sent - `s.queued()`. The speakers trail it by up to one device
  buffer (~N ms at 48 kHz).
- Seek or stop: `s.clear()` drops the queue at once, then queue from the new spot. Scrubbing is
  the same: `clear()` and queue a short grain (20-N ms) at the cursor each drag step.
- `s.pause(true/false)` holds the device; queued samples wait. `s.close()` at the end.
- SDL_mixer (`Sound`, `Music`) is a separate device; both play at the same time.
- `SDL_AUDIODRIVER=dummy` drains in real time, so `queued()` counts down in headless tests.
  The `game_headless` backend (`j3c check`) gives an empty stream.

==> j3.toml <==
[package]
name = "tone"
entry = "src/main.j3"

[link]
libs = ["SDL2"]

==> src/main.j3 <==
module tone;

use j3.game;
use j3.io.printLn;
use j3.math.{ TAU, sin };
use j3.memory.Arena;

const RATE: int = 48000;
const AHEAD: int = 2400; // keep N ms queued

fn main() {
    let s = game.openAudioStream(RATE, 2);
    if s.raw == 0 {
        printLn("no audio device");
        return;
    }
    let arena = Arena.create(1024 * 1024);
    let buf = arena.alloc::<f32>(AHEAD * 2);
    let phase: f32 = 0;
    let sent = 0; // frames handed to the device
    let start = game.ticks();
    let last = start;
    while game.ticks() - start < 2000 {
        // One "frame": top the queue back up to AHEAD frames.
        let n = AHEAD - s.queued();
        if n > 0 {
            for i in 0..n {
                let v = 0.2 * sin(phase);
                buf[i * 2] = v;
                buf[i * 2 + 1] = v;
                phase = phase + TAU * 440.0 / f32(RATE);
                if phase > TAU { phase = phase - TAU; }
            }
            s.queue(buf[0..n * 2]);
            sent = sent + n;
        }
        if game.ticks() - last >= 250 {
            last = game.ticks();
            // Playhead: what the device has taken so far, to within one 512-frame buffer.
            printLn(`playhead {sent - s.queued()} frames`);
        }
        while game.ticks() - last < 16 && game.ticks() - start < 2000 {}
    }
    s.clear(); // instant stop; a seek is clear() then queue from the new spot
    s.close();
}
